# Pairs with MonotonicVisibility. This is the orphan guard itself: removing the
# fall-through means a late reshard shadow-forward bucket SHADOWS the
# authoritative projection instead of deferring to it, so a key that was
# readable at its post-saga value reverts to the pre-saga value. This is the
# #1584 defect class at design level, and the reason AlreadyTerminal is an
# input to the gate at all.
MODULE: MonotonicVisibilityOrphanShadows
TARGET: MonotonicVisibility
CLASS: Action
SUMMARY: lets a late reshard orphan bucket shadow the committed projection, so a visible key reverts

--- FIND
ObservedPrepared(t, k) ==
    IF pend[t][k] = "pending"
    THEN IF SurfaceViaGate(t, k) THEN TRUE ELSE ProjectedPrepared(t, k)
    ELSE ProjectedPrepared(t, k)
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the pending branch no longer falls through to the authoritative
\* projection when the gate refuses it. A shadow-forward orphan arriving after
\* the leaf applied its commit terminal therefore hides the committed value.
ObservedPrepared(t, k) ==
    IF pend[t][k] = "pending"
    THEN SurfaceViaGate(t, k)
    ELSE ProjectedPrepared(t, k)
--- END
